      "review_notes": "The canonical finite mixture chooses each logarithmic magnitude level equally; zero has its own bucket, positive buckets are inclusive power intervals, and the final bucket is clipped to the inclusive maximum. This is an exact integer bucket law, with no continuous log-density claim. Named natural-log inequalities prove all positive buckets are valid. Deterministic ceiling and integer-power helpers keep the CTE proof symbolic. Tests check maximum0 Dirac0, base2 maxima7 and8 bucket boundaries, exact mass1/5 at the clipped final singleton8, arbitrary infinite expectation and framed clients."
    }
